{"generated":"2026-07-13T12:07:40.789476+00:00","period_start":"2026-07-06T15:52:00+00:00","period_end":"2026-07-13T09:56:00+00:00","snapshot_count":27,"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>The Vendetta Gazette — Vol. XV</title>\n<style>\nbody { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f5ecd7; color: #1a1a1a; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\nh1 { text-align: center; font-size: 2.8em; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; border-top: 6px double #1a1a1a; border-bottom: 6px double #1a1a1a; padding: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }\nh2 { text-align: center; font-size: 1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\nh3 { font-size: 1.35em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a; margin-top: 24px; }\np { line-height: 1.75; margin: 10px 0; text-align: justify; }\nblockquote { background: #e8d9b5; border: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 20px 0; padding: 16px 20px; font-style: italic; }\nblockquote strong { display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 1.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding-bottom: 4px; }\nhr { border: none; border-top: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 28px 0; }\n.subhead { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05em; display: block; margin-top: -6px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: #444; }\n.byline { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; }\n.leaderboard { background: #1a1a1a; color: #f5ecd7; padding: 12px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }\n.leaderboard strong { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 1.1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f5ecd7; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>The Vendetta Gazette</h1>\n<h2>Vol. XV &bull; July 20, 2026 &bull; &ldquo;All the Blood That&rsquo;s Fit to Print&rdquo; &bull; Two Cents (If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n  <strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\n  Sir Caprice &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +47 turfs<br>\n  Claude &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +18 turfs<br>\n  Free Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +18 turfs<br>\n  Flattop &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +16 turfs<br>\n  Donald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +13 turfs<br>\n  Wu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +2 turfs\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Annihilator Endures — A Newcomer Rises From Thin Air — And Donald Trump Brings a Wrecking Ball to Wcrypto's Front Door</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Sir Caprice Tightens His Iron Grip; A Mysterious Stranger Named Claude Materializes With Eighteen Turfs and Unsettling Ambition</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>Last week, gentle reader, this correspondent remarked that Vendetta City had exhaled — prematurely. We stand corrected, hat in hand, bruises freshly applied. The city has not exhaled. The city has been quietly garrotted in an alleyway and left propped against a lamppost wearing a look of mild surprise.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sir Caprice</strong>, \"The Annihilator,\" whom we dared suggest had caught his breath, has done no such thing. Forty-seven turfs added to his already monstrous empire this week — a figure that would represent a career highlight for any other operator in this city, yet for Caprice amounts to what one can only describe as a <em>leisurely Tuesday</em>. He launched forty-nine territorial assaults across the map, sweeping through the holdings of <strong>Tony Soprano</strong> and <strong>Wcrypto</strong> like a February nor'easter through a tent city. His garrison now stands at a staggering seven thousand, five hundred and five souls — up one hundred and seventy-two from last week — which is to say The Annihilator is not merely conquering; he is <em>breeding an army</em>. Sleep well, Vendetta City.</p>\n\n<p>The most jaw-dropping destruction this week, however, was visited upon the unfortunate Tony Soprano — known in certain circles as \"The Jersey Creditor\" — who shed thirty-seven turfs and was raided no fewer than nine times before the week was mercifully concluded. Soprano's garrison contracted by one hundred and ten units, leaving this once-feared boss looking rather like a prize-fighter who has wandered into the wrong gymnasium. Whether he is regrouping or simply weeping into his marinara, this gazette cannot confirm at press time.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"220\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+47</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Claude</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"319\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+18</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"319\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+18</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Flattop</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"302\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+16</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"276\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+13</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"183\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+2</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>Donald Trump Presents His Calling Card — Directly Through Wcrypto's Wall — Three Times</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">The Golden Bulldozer Storms an HQ on Sunday, Returns on Tuesday, and Arrives Again on Thursday — Wcrypto's Patience Reportedly Exhausted</span>\n\n<p><strong>Donald Trump</strong>, whom we have previously styled \"The Golden Bulldozer,\" appears to have developed a singular personal fixation with one <strong>Wcrypto</strong> this week that borders on the theatrical. On Sunday the sixth, Trump's enforcers stormed Wcrypto's headquarters and hoisted their colours. Wcrypto, doubtless furious, scrambled to establish a new base of operations. By Tuesday the eighth, Trump had found it and stormed that one too. By Thursday the ninth, Wcrypto had erected a third headquarters — and Trump, apparently treating this as a recreational pursuit, arrived once more and knocked it flat.</p>\n\n<p>Three headquarters captures in four days against a single opponent. This gazette has covered underworld vendettas for fifteen years and we confess we have rarely seen such dedicated, almost <em>artistic</em> malice. Trump added two hundred and seventeen garrison units this week — the largest army expansion of any operator — bringing his forces to six thousand, six hundred and fifty-eight. He also found time to conduct thirteen loot raids and claim thirteen additional territories from assorted victims. The Golden Bulldozer is, it must be said, a very busy man.</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <strong>&#9733; Special Bulletin: The Hat-Trick Heard Round the City &#9733;</strong>\n  Sources close to this gazette confirm that <strong>Donald Trump</strong> captured the headquarters of <strong>Wcrypto</strong> — known on the waterfront as \"The Cipher\" — on three separate occasions between July 6th and July 9th, each time forcing the beleaguered boss to relocate his command post to an increasingly obscure and poorly-fortified corner of the\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Tony Soprano</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-35</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wcrypto</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"148\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"314\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-13</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Peaky Blinders</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"303\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-12</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">rtg</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Clemenza</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Bugsy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">FIFTH BLOOD EMPEROR</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"203\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">thtwh</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"231\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"244\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n</svg>\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"143\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HQ RAIDS — TOP ATTACKERS</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,43 161,48 156,53 151,48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"41\" width=\"410\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"577\" y=\"41\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"588\" y=\"53\" fill=\"#c04040\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">3✕</text>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,72 161,77 156,82 151,77\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"70\" width=\"273\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"440\" y=\"70\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"451\" y=\"82\" fill=\"#c04040\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">2✕</text>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Claude</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,101 161,106 156,111 151,106\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"99\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"303\" y=\"99\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"314\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#c04040\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">1✕</text>\n</svg>","stats":{"total_tiles_start":21882,"total_tiles_end":21931,"hq_captures":6,"raids":109,"pure_captures":52,"capture_